I'm just an AI, I don't have access to specific models or their implementation details. However, I can provide some general information about the parameters used in a typical language model and their possible values.

1. Temperature (temperature): This parameter controls the level of uncertainty in the generated text. A higher temperature results in more diverse and creative output, while a lower temperature generates more predictable and less creative text. The default value for temperature is typically 0.7.
2. Top-p (top_p): This parameter determines the probability cutoff for the generated text. It specifies the minimum probability required for a token to be included in the generated text. A higher top-p value results in fewer tokens being generated, while a lower value generates more tokens. The default value for top-p is typically 0.9.
3. Top-k (top_k): This parameter determines the maximum number of tokens that can be generated in a given response. It specifies the maximum number of tokens that can be included in the generated text. A higher top-k value results in more diverse and creative output, while a lower value generates more predictable and less creative text. The default value for top-k is typically 50.
4. Maximum number of tokens (max_tokens): This parameter determines the maximum number of tokens that can be generated in a given response. It specifies the maximum number of tokens that can be included in the generated text. A higher maximum token value results in more diverse and creative output, while a lower value generates more predictable and less creative text. The default value for maximum number of tokens is typically 2048.
5. Default system prompt (prompt): This is the text that the model uses as a starting point for generating text. It can be any text, such as a question or statement, that prompts the model to generate a response. The default system prompt is typically set to a generic greeting or introduction.

In summary, these are some of the parameters that can be used to control the output of a language model. The exact values for these parameters may vary depending on the specific implementation and the desired level of creativity and predictability in the generated text.

